  "construction": {
    "basis": "reconstruction",
    "fidelity": "not-applicable",
    "note": "The finished design was read from Wichmann’s F207 drawing, whose pieces are drawn edge to edge. The decagons sit at the centre and the corners of a rectangle whose sides are in the ratio of 1 to tan 36°. Every line is one of 25 lines about a decagon: the five lines through its centre and its corners, the lines of its ten sides, and the lines of the sides of the decagon of radius √5 about it (drawing within 0.001 of OA). The decagons at the tile’s corners get their lines by mirroring those about O. The drawing gives no steps; we devised the construction.",
    "changes": "The compass steps, their order and the named points are ours. Colours follow the shapes; the screen itself is white marble with no colour. No photograph was checked.",
    "reviewed": "2026-10-27"
  },
